To demonstrate the problems with existing samplers, we choose a structured transition matrix $A$:  egin{equation} A_{ij}= egin{cases} p & j=i\ 1-p & j=(i+1)	ext{ mod }S\ 0 & 	ext{otherwise}. \end{cases} \end{equation} At each position, the token $x^d$ has probability $p$ of staying fixed and probability $1-p$ of changing into the next token. To evaluate sample quality, one important metric is the number of errors in the samples, i.e., occurrences of impossible transitions within the sampled sequence. The overall error rate is computed by: 
